      ],
      "confirmed": "Three complete source files read. FrameIndex samples fractions i/(count+1), reduced via GCD, no ctor input validation; equality structural rationalpair, externally supplied equivalent fractions not normalized; zero denominator/overflow count+1 unguarded here. Candidate unordered pair hash symmetric but mutable File1/File2 can invalidate hashset membership; equality assumes distinct files, selfpair could break equivalence if accepted upstream. TryStartProcessing locks both files atomically under caller supplied shared lock, StopProcessing atomic writes; lifecycle cleanup pending engine review. No C# build/runtime/media comparison run, no algorithm adoption."
    },
    {
      "paths": [
        "ComparisonManager/Comparison.cs",
        "ComparisonManager/ComparisonManager.cs"
      ],
      "confirmed": "Two complete sources read. Explicit Aborted/Cancelled results positive error-state pattern. Cancelled LastComparedIndex uses last.LoadLevel whereas exception uses last.Index and regular result frame index; inconsistent cursor semantics. Frame comparison list retains full frames and GetStatus copies suffix unbounded, no response/memory budget or validated negative cursor. Manager active comparison count unlimited, task launches before registration.5min timeout based lastpoll DateTime.Now (wallclock, clients can keepalive forever), cancellation Dispose.Wait indefinite under global manager lock can stall all status/start/cancel/cleanup. Cancel removes result immediately, later status null instead of retained terminal outcome. File.Exists before decode no stable identity snapshot. No runtime/build or adoption."
    },
    {
      "paths": [
        "DedupEngine/EngineDatastore.cs",
        "DedupEngine/ThrottledEvent.cs",
        "DedupEngine/ThrottledOperationUpdate.cs"
