      "confirmed": "Three whole sources read. Duration cache key only basename+size+Unixmtime, different directories with same attributes collide; algorithm/contentversion/fileidentity absent. Insert stores TotalSeconds(double) into INTEGER-affinity column while retrieval GetInt64, fractional precision behavior requires realSqlite control, no runtime claim. Unique conflict IGNORE retains first duration, no invalidation/lifecycle/pruning here. Throttle uses Utc wallclock rather than monotonic, initial100ms suppressed and no trailing/latest update queue; last progress can be dropped unless engine explicit terminalevent (pending review). Atomic compareexchange limits concurrent emission, but caller callback inline exceptions unhandled here. No datastore opened, no UI/runtime or source adoption."
    },
    {
      "paths": [
        "VideoComparer/VideoFile.cs",
        "VideoComparer/ComparisonException.cs",
        "VideoComparer/EventArgs/ComparisonFinishedEventArgs.cs",
        "VideoComparer/EventArgs/FrameComparedEventArgs.cs"
      ],
      "confirmed": "Four complete pinned sources read and Git blob hashes verified. VideoFile identity uses raw path string only. File metadata errors collapse to cached zero or MinValue, duration decode failure to cached zero; no stable content snapshot or explicit incomplete state here. Percent duration tolerance scales only with left duration and is asymmetric; strict less-than with zero tolerance rejects identical durations. Copying frame dictionary shares mutable byte arrays; public frame storage has no resource bound here. IVideoFile copy constructor dereferences other before null guard. Event payloads mutable and no run provenance in these types. Source inspection only; no C# build, original tests, FFmpeg execution or adoption."
    },
    {
      "paths": [
        "VideoComparer/VideoComparer.cs"
      ],
      "confirmed": "Whole 646-line source read, Git blob verified. AVX2 widened short comparison produces two byte mask bits per differing pixel; PopCount sum divides by256 without halving, so maximum difference2 rather than1. Portable Vector<byte> subtraction wraps before Abs, so left0/right255 yields1 rather than255 and can fall below threshold3. Native C# execution not performed. Memory cache wrappers always default Loaded=false even on TryGetValue success, so reread DB/file unless datastore returns it. LoadFramesFromFile enumerates lazy frame preprocessing once to cache and again on consumption, recreating bitmap pipeline with GC.Collect each time. Frame preprocessing crops black bars, nearest downsamples16x16, grayscale byte threshold3: heuristic similarity, not exact file or full-video identity. Null frames count as differences but no-result fallback becomes Duplicate; zero CompareCount yields no comparisons then Duplicate absent caller validation. ForceLoadingAllFrames continues and overwrites prior terminal result at later levels; earlier Different may be lost if later level empty/NoResult, pending caller settings validation. Static datastore cache unbounded/no disposal here; event serialization stores original and intermediate streams; no pixel or total memory budget here. No code adoption or upstream tests."
    },
